# RPC boundary-call counts per call (req 19), taken with campaign_rpc_count against campaign_server on a Unix socket,
# 4 calls per cell and job (2 for d), averaged. The gate (run_campaign.sh gate) diffs the '^  [BCDE]' rows against this file.
# forward = rpc + codec + host:
#   rpc   : the core's RPC entry points (ak_call_unary, ak_call_unary_enc, ak_enc_take_owned, ak_call_open, ak_call_send,
#           ak_call_send_enc, ak_call_recv, ak_call_destroy, ak_bytes_free), counted by the core's counting build;
#   codec : core codec entry points (forward) and reverse calls into the host (reverse), same counters;
#   host  : ak_enc_reset / ak_dec_reset counted in the binding under AK_COUNTING. Place: an encode resets once, before it;
#           a retain decode resets ONCE, before it (decision 11 rule 7; its context stays armed); a drop decode makes none.
#           Retain: no pre-placed buffer, the binding's geometric unk_grow (rule 8).
# Jobs: a = Fetch P2.2 (decode on the client; a+read adds no boundary call, not listed); b = Push P2.2; c = Upload P5.3 /
# P5.4 (unary, empty response); d = UploadStream 4 MiB / 16 MiB in 2 MiB M5 chunks (client streaming, UploadAck response).
# Re-taken 2026-09-27 for FIX-PLAN WP8, against the 2026-09-26 file:
#   - retain decodes 1 forward lower (one reset): C-retain a 5 -> 4, D-retain a 3 -> 2;
#   - cell C sends with ak_call_unary_enc (the encode context moved, as the Rust slice) instead of ak_enc_take + a copy
#     into ak_call_unary: C b 2515 -> 2514 (drop), 2521 -> 2520 (retain);
#   - cell D hands grpc++ the core's buffer with ak_enc_take_owned (moved; released with ak_bytes_free when grpc++ drops
#     it) instead of ak_enc_take + a copy: D b rpc 0 -> 2, D b 2513 -> 2514 (drop), 2519 -> 2520 (retain);
#   - new: framed twins Bf, Cf-* and Ef-* (ak_client_set_framed), identical to their reference rows; jobs c and d.
# Re-taken 2026-09-28 (req. 16 as amended: C++ core cells on blocking AND the completion queue): NEW rows only, for the
#   queue cells B-q, Bf-q, C-q-*, Cf-q-*, E-q-*, Ef-q-* (one ak_queue per cell, the issuing thread drains it); every
#   earlier row identical. rpc also counts ak_call_unary_q, ak_call_unary_enc_q, ak_call_send_q, ak_call_send_enc_q,
#   ak_call_recv_q and ak_queue_next. Per call a queue cell adds ak_queue_next per completion and ak_call_destroy
#   (unary: B a/b/c 2 -> 4, C c 4 -> 6; d: one ak_queue_next per send and one for the recv, B d 6 -> 9 / 12 -> 21).
# A and F make no core call (grpc++ only); E uses the core's transport with the host-generated codec, so codec is 0.
